COX-2) enzymes leading to the formation ofvarious prostaglandins (PGs). Certain PUFAs and PGs can also activate PPAR-<italic>&#x003b3;</italic>. Selective and nonselective COX-2 inhibitors(COX Inh) block PG formation by COX-2 but can also at higher concentrationsactivate PPAR-<italic>&#x003b3;</italic>. Solid arrows indicate activation; dashedarrow indicates metabolic pathway; blocked arrow indicates inhibition.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="PPAR2008-326915.001"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>